course: dictionary
lesson: 6395
title: Munch: eating with noise and joy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To munch means to chew food steadily and noisily, often with enjoyment. «The caterpillar munched through the leaves.» You can hear the chewing and picture the caterpillar enjoying its meal, so munch paints a clearer picture than just ate.
explain: Munch is a good word for your own stories. Try swapping it in: «The rabbit ate the carrot» becomes «The rabbit munched the carrot». Ask yourself: does my meaning still fit the sentence? If it does, the swap works.
explain: Munch changes form: munches, munched and munching. Phrases such as munch on and munch away are common: «The panda munches for up to 14 hours a day.» Slang uses the munchies to mean feeling very hungry for snacks.
explain: Watch the capital letter. «Edvard Munch» is a person's name, a Norwegian painter who made «The Scream». The clues around the word tell you whether it is an action, a snack, or a name.
fact: «Munch» means to chew steadily and noisily, often with enjoyment.
fact: «The munchies» is slang for feeling very hungry for snacks.
fact: In informal speech, a munch can mean a snack or a meal, as in «Let's grab some munch.»
fact: Edvard Munch, from Norway, made several versions of «The Scream» from 1893.
fact: A silverback gorilla munches about 18 kilograms of leaves a day.
exercise: «The caterpillar munched through the leaves.» What does munched mean? | *Chewed steadily and noisily | Fell asleep | Jumped over | Hid under a flowerpot
exercise: Priya says, «I've got the munchies.» What does she mean? | *She feels very hungry for snacks | She is looking for her lost dog | She has lost her lunch box | She has a tummy ache
exercise: In «Edvard Munch, from Norway, made several versions of The Scream», what is Munch? | A snack | A kind of bamboo | *A painter's name | A chewing sound
test: Which word is the best swap for ate in a lively story about a hungry dog? | *munched | ran | slept | left
test: «The giant panda munches for up to 14 hours a day.» How long can a panda munch in one day? | Two seconds | One whole week | *Up to 14 hours | Ten minutes
exam: In «Let's grab some munch», munch means | A painting | *A snack or meal | A tree | A noisy chewing sound
